# Lazav, Wearer of Faces: its attack trigger exiles for good, not "until Lazav leaves the battlefield" (CR 610.3 does not apply).
# It exiles the Ornithopter on turn 3; on turn 4 Bot2 kills Lazav with a Lightning Bolt (3 damage to a 2/3). The Ornithopter stays in
# exile and does not come back to the graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Lazav, Wearer of Faces
Ornithopter
Lightning Bolt
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lazav, Wearer of Faces.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Lazav, Wearer of Faces > Bot2)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Graveyard.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Exile = Ornithopter
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Lazav, Wearer of Faces)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Lazav, Wearer of Faces = (absent)
Bot1.Graveyard = Lazav, Wearer of Faces; Lightning Bolt
Exile = Ornithopter
